  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How are you?",
   "texto": [
    "**Wie geht's?** is the short form of **Wie geht es dir?** (how are you doing?). With «Sie»: **Wie geht es Ihnen?**",
    "**Gut, danke** (well, thank you) or **Sehr gut** (very well) is answered. Other answers: **Es geht** (regular), **Nicht so gut** (not very good).",
    "To return the question: **Und dir?** or **Und Ihnen?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Present someone",
   "texto": [
    "**Das ist Paul** (this is Paul). «Das ist» is for men, women and things.",
    "**Er** is «He» and **sie** (with a tiny) is «her.».",
    "In German the subject is **obligatorio**: you can't just say «ist müde»; you have to say **Er ist müde** (you're tired)."
   ]
